;; The module _uuid (py-design-1122): Modules/_uuidmodule.c of CPython 3.14.10 as a build with libuuid has it on Linux,
;; uuid.py's _generate_time_safe (test_uuid's TestUUIDWithExtModule and TestInternalsWithExtModule skip without it):
;; generate_time_safe() returns uuid_generate_time_safe's 16 bytes and status as (bytes, int), the status 0 when the
;; UUID was made in a safe way (libuuid's state file under its lock, or uuidd) and -1 otherwise: here always -1, one
;; process's clock sequence, as libuuid without a writable /var/lib/libuuid and no uuidd gives. The UUID is libuuid's
;; time-based version 1 (util-linux's gen_uuid.c, read as prior art, nothing vendored): the 100-ns intervals since
;; 1582-10-15, a 14-bit clock sequence drawn at random once and advanced when the clock goes back, up to 10 UUIDs a
;; tick (UUIDS_PER_TICK) by the adjustment added to the time, the variant bits 10, and as node the hardware address of
;; the first interface that has a non-zero 6-byte one (get_node_id), else 48 random bits with the multicast bit set.
;; has_uuid_generate_time_safe is 1; has_stable_extractable_node (configure's check that two runs' nodes are equal) is
;; 1 when the node is an interface's address, which is the same in every process, else 0.

